WEBVTT

00:01.544 --> 00:04.757
<i>♪ it seems today
 that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.843 --> 00:07.973
<i>♪ is violence in movies
 and sex on tv ♪</i>

00:08.142 --> 00:11.689
<i>♪ but where are those
 good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.774 --> 00:14.696
<i>♪ on which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.781 --> 00:18.162
<i>♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.247 --> 00:21.294
<i>♪ lucky there's a man who
 positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.421 --> 00:23.048
<i>♪ all the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.133 --> 00:24.300
<i>♪ laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.427 --> 00:30.271
<i>♪ he's... A...
 Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:36.788 --> 00:37.871
Boy, everybody's here.

00:37.956 --> 00:39.333
Why do you think
we're gathering?

00:39.460 --> 00:41.922
This isn't about the soiled
pants in the toilet, right?

00:42.007 --> 00:43.175
'cause I hadn't heard
about that.

00:43.260 --> 00:44.762
Good morning, employees.

00:44.847 --> 00:46.766
As some of you can tell
by my face,

00:46.851 --> 00:48.186
I have some exciting news.

00:48.271 --> 00:50.900
But first, a pair of husky-size
green pants were found

00:50.985 --> 00:53.364
In the men's room,
positively destroyed.

00:53.491 --> 00:55.076
(whispers): That's what
I hadn't heard about.

00:55.203 --> 00:56.746
Now the exciting news.

00:56.832 --> 00:59.085
The brewery is transitioning
to an open floor plan

00:59.170 --> 01:01.799
And will be called
the pawtucket patriot campus.

01:01.884 --> 01:04.638
To help explain the transition
to our futuristic workplace,

01:04.765 --> 01:06.685
I'd like to share a video
from our investor,

01:06.770 --> 01:09.899
The confusingly charismatic
wework lunatic.

01:10.027 --> 01:12.196
<i> Hey, I'm the guy from wework.</i>

01:12.323 --> 01:14.160
<i> My foremost goal is
 to facilitate</i>

01:14.287 --> 01:16.832
<i> An experiential bandwidth
 of synergy.</i>

01:16.917 --> 01:18.919
<i> Hammock desks,
 scooter desks,</i>

01:19.005 --> 01:21.216
<i>And the world's first desk-desk.</i>

01:21.385 --> 01:24.223
<i> The only desk that
 functions as a working desk.</i>

01:24.309 --> 01:27.271
<i>I have been the wework lunatic,
 please don't google me.</i>

01:27.356 --> 01:29.610
Our new office will also have

01:29.695 --> 01:31.614
A lady chef
who only makes vegan food,

01:31.699 --> 01:34.119
Pinball machines,
and nursing pods.

01:34.205 --> 01:37.126
Lastly, as we transition
to our new open floor plan,

01:37.212 --> 01:38.504
The brewery will be closed

01:38.632 --> 01:40.258
For the next two months
for construction.

01:40.302 --> 01:41.385
Yes, griffin?

01:41.512 --> 01:45.394
Are the nursing pods,
l-like, for anyone?

01:49.321 --> 01:51.241
If I ordered
a whole cornish game hen,

01:51.326 --> 01:52.368
Would anyone have any?

01:52.453 --> 01:54.288
I'm in for a wing.
What's the occasion?

01:54.416 --> 01:56.252
I just found out
the brewery's closing

01:56.337 --> 01:57.922
So they can turn it into
the kind of workplace

01:58.007 --> 01:59.801
You only see on tv shows.

01:59.928 --> 02:01.554
Work's been crazy for me, too.

02:01.640 --> 02:03.810
We have this case--
guy died on his birthday,

02:03.895 --> 02:05.355
And-- get this--
his family had gotten him

02:05.440 --> 02:06.524
An ice cream cake.

02:06.609 --> 02:08.528
You know, the kind
with ice cream inside

02:08.613 --> 02:09.739
As the cake part?

02:09.866 --> 02:11.535
(laughs)

02:11.620 --> 02:14.207
Wild stuff.
So I'm at the scene...

02:14.293 --> 02:16.169
This story is already
too complicated and boring.

02:16.256 --> 02:17.339
Peter, take over.

02:17.425 --> 02:19.051
My amazon guy
once delivered batteries

02:19.178 --> 02:21.348
-To pat sajak.
-No way!

02:21.392 --> 02:23.602
How did he know there were
batteries in the box?

02:23.772 --> 02:25.106
You know,
whenever they ship a battery,

02:25.233 --> 02:27.027
They got to put that little
warning label on the box?

02:27.155 --> 02:28.613
That's how.

02:28.741 --> 02:30.577
It could've just been something
with a battery in it.

02:30.704 --> 02:32.539
No, he said
he shook it real hard.

02:32.708 --> 02:34.543
I-I think
the focus of this story is

02:34.628 --> 02:36.757
More pat sajak than
the battery part.

02:36.884 --> 02:40.515
Hold on. There's no way
that story was better than mine.

02:42.521 --> 02:44.690
Hey, brian. What's all this?

02:44.777 --> 02:46.445
Oh, just following
in the rich tradition

02:46.530 --> 02:48.074
Of hemingway and faulkner

02:48.192 --> 02:49.786
And putting a little damage
on the old liver.

02:49.913 --> 02:51.205
Another rosé, brian?

02:51.332 --> 02:52.583
Put a spritz on it.

02:52.668 --> 02:56.374
So, is, uh, watching tiktoks
of underage girls

02:56.426 --> 02:58.429
Also part of
your writing process?

02:58.515 --> 03:01.686
The best writing happens when
you're not actually writing.

03:01.814 --> 03:03.732
I just wish
my muse would speak to me.

03:03.818 --> 03:06.572
I'm having a tough time finding
an idea for my next novel.

03:06.741 --> 03:10.080
Well, I'd tell you about
one of my murder cases,

03:10.165 --> 03:12.460
But apparently
I'm a bad storyteller.

03:12.587 --> 03:15.466
-Murder case?
-Oh, yeah, we had one last year.

03:15.593 --> 03:17.763
All signs pointed
to the husband.

03:17.849 --> 03:19.517
-What happened?
-It was the husband.

03:19.602 --> 03:22.064
You know, we have
a whole file of cases in quahog

03:22.150 --> 03:24.068
That would make great stories.

03:24.196 --> 03:26.490
A lot of murdered women
out there, bri.

03:26.576 --> 03:28.704
Half of them named britney,
half of them named lacey.

03:28.789 --> 03:31.251
That's one piece of advice
I always give young parents:

03:31.378 --> 03:33.046
Don't name them
britney or lacey.

03:33.132 --> 03:34.258
Yeah, sad stuff.

03:34.385 --> 03:36.220
You know, true crime is huge
right now.

03:36.306 --> 03:37.724
You could be
sitting on a gold mine.

03:37.767 --> 03:39.185
A gold mine, huh?

03:39.271 --> 03:42.484
And this whole day I thought
it was just a smushed dook.

03:45.074 --> 03:47.286
<i> Announcer (on tv):
 We now return to
curb your enthusiasm,</i>

03:47.371 --> 03:50.752
<i> Where jeff garlin just repeats
 everything larry says.</i>

03:50.879 --> 03:52.673
<i> So, I put on the shirt.</i>

03:52.842 --> 03:54.594
<i> You put on the shirt!</i>

03:54.721 --> 03:56.013
<i> I paid for it.</i>

03:56.099 --> 03:57.683
<i> You paid for it!</i>

03:57.853 --> 04:00.105
<i> I'm starting to think
 you're, uh,</i>

04:00.234 --> 04:02.152
<i> The weakest link in the cast.</i>

04:02.238 --> 04:04.699
<i> Easily the weakest link!</i>

04:04.785 --> 04:07.413
Peter, the bank called
to say we're overdrawn,

04:07.541 --> 04:09.417
And the credit card company
sent us a letter

04:09.546 --> 04:11.673
That just says:
"bitch better have my money."

04:11.758 --> 04:12.926
Visa sent that?

04:13.053 --> 04:14.680
God, they can do
whatever they want in delaware.

04:14.765 --> 04:16.642
Thanks for nothing, sleepy joe.

04:16.769 --> 04:19.439
I wonder if this has anything
to do with me not getting paid

04:19.526 --> 04:21.151
During the brewery renovations.

04:21.280 --> 04:23.490
Wh-what do you mean
"not getting paid"?

04:23.576 --> 04:25.327
Well, preston said
we're all transitioning

04:25.371 --> 04:27.039
To being
independent contractors.

04:27.126 --> 04:29.086
The downside is we're losing
our health insurance,

04:29.171 --> 04:32.050
But there's gonna be a pinball
machine in the break room.

04:32.137 --> 04:33.930
Peter, we can't afford
to go two months

04:34.016 --> 04:35.559
Without your paycheck.

04:35.644 --> 04:37.813
You're gonna have to
find a job in the meantime.

04:37.898 --> 04:40.778
Lois, don't worry.
I got it all figured out.

04:40.905 --> 04:43.367
(shoes tapping)

04:52.013 --> 04:54.141
"dear mr. Griffin,
we regret to inform you

04:54.310 --> 04:56.395
That we cannot offer you
a space."

04:57.484 --> 05:00.656
-(shoes tapping)
-(singsongy): Another big
dance check in the mail.

05:00.741 --> 05:04.497
I was just five years away
from three figures a month.

05:04.624 --> 05:06.794
(shoes tapping slowly)

05:12.182 --> 05:13.308
Joe, this stuff is great.

05:13.435 --> 05:15.604
Yep, one man's murdered,
estranged wife

05:15.690 --> 05:17.191
Is another man's treasure.

05:17.276 --> 05:20.490
Brian, I'm gonna have to ask you
to put down the severed limb.

05:20.617 --> 05:22.077
I brought this from home.

05:22.204 --> 05:24.039
Drop it. Drop it!

05:24.126 --> 05:27.213
Ah, damn it, you said "drop it,"
so now I got to drop it.

05:27.340 --> 05:30.095
You know, we should team up
and write a true crime novel.

05:30.222 --> 05:31.347
You don't happen to have
any cases

05:31.433 --> 05:33.226
Featuring pretty blonde women,
do you?

05:33.396 --> 05:34.771
No, those get solved
pretty quickly.

05:34.898 --> 05:37.987
This victim was brunette
and a little heavy.

05:38.114 --> 05:39.574
Okay, getting warmer.

05:39.659 --> 05:42.413
We'll just change a few
key details so people care.

05:42.498 --> 05:44.418
Gutierrez?
Nope, gordon.

05:44.536 --> 05:46.380
Murdered on
an indian reservation?

05:46.466 --> 05:47.759
Let's try beverly hills.

05:47.927 --> 05:50.598
I'm thinking we go novel,
podcast, docuseries,

05:50.683 --> 05:52.518
Then full-blown blockbuster.

05:52.604 --> 05:55.317
But we'd also be doing this
for the families, right?

05:55.402 --> 05:56.811
Is that a new
streaming platform?

05:56.864 --> 05:58.574
No, like, the families
of the victims?

05:58.659 --> 05:59.826
Oh, right. Yeah, sure.

06:00.037 --> 06:02.415
In fact, we'll give them
a sliver of the proceeds.

06:02.584 --> 06:04.545
And I'll give
the fictional version

06:04.631 --> 06:06.132
Of their daughter bigger boobs.

06:06.259 --> 06:07.803
Like-like real heavy naturals.

06:07.846 --> 06:11.101
Oh, yeah, that sounds
like a good compromise.

06:15.028 --> 06:16.738
Your special cart, mrs. G.

06:16.824 --> 06:19.369
Just gave the wheels
a fresh coat of wd-40.

06:19.454 --> 06:21.749
Why, thank you, james.

06:22.921 --> 06:26.133
Oh, roberto, if you weren't
missing half an arm,

06:26.262 --> 06:27.554
I'd definitely consider it.

06:27.639 --> 06:30.184
Oh, how's the 6029s today, hmm?

06:30.311 --> 06:32.565
Oh, mrs. Lois, very fresh.

06:32.650 --> 06:34.318
What's she talking about, mommy?

06:34.445 --> 06:36.155
(laughs) kale, dear.

06:36.241 --> 06:38.787
It's insider speak for kale.

06:44.509 --> 06:46.303
That can't possibly be a thing.

06:46.389 --> 06:48.934
Let me just find someone
to make sure.

06:51.358 --> 06:54.654
Oh, looks like someone
got pulled from the night shift

06:54.741 --> 06:57.453
'cause I've never seen
this free sample.

06:58.874 --> 07:01.169
<i>-Peter?!
 -Man (over speakers):
 Ladies and gentlemen,</i>

07:01.296 --> 07:03.048
<i> We have a plot twist
 on aisle four.</i>

07:03.217 --> 07:05.721
<i> I'm the assistant manager
 who thinks work should be fun,</i>

07:05.806 --> 07:07.850
<i> And definitely not
 a corporate spy</i>

07:08.019 --> 07:09.604
<i> Here to keep unions
 from forming.</i>

07:09.731 --> 07:11.441
<i> But now that
 we're talking about it,</i>

07:11.569 --> 07:12.903
<i> Can you imagine
 if you had a grievance</i>

07:12.988 --> 07:14.950
<i> And couldn't talk to me
 directly?</i>

07:15.077 --> 07:16.410
<i> Anyway, I'm elliot,</i>

07:16.496 --> 07:17.872
<i> And I'm paying close attention</i>

07:17.958 --> 07:20.211
<i> To who posts what
 on the break room cork board.</i>

07:26.267 --> 07:27.769
Peter, what are you doing here?

07:27.896 --> 07:29.523
You told me to get a job,
and they were hiring.

07:29.650 --> 07:30.483
I love it here!

07:30.610 --> 07:31.653
Plus, they let me joke around

07:31.738 --> 07:33.949
With the wells fargo guys
who work here.

07:34.034 --> 07:36.789
Yes, I'd like to make
a deposit, please.

07:36.874 --> 07:39.670
Is it another 100 grand
chocolate bar?

07:39.755 --> 07:41.632
Okay, so I've had you before.

07:41.676 --> 07:44.597
Peter, the grocery store is
kind of my domain.

07:44.683 --> 07:46.476
While I'm glad you got a job,

07:46.562 --> 07:48.398
I don't love
that you got one here.

07:48.483 --> 07:49.859
Don't worry.
You won't even know I'm here.

07:49.986 --> 07:51.404
Unless you're
near the front door,

07:51.489 --> 07:53.241
Which I can open
with the force.

07:53.326 --> 07:55.413
Excuse me,
where are the peanuts?

07:55.498 --> 07:56.833
Aisle seven.

07:56.960 --> 07:58.920
Peter, peanuts are on aisle two.

07:59.006 --> 08:00.174
Eh, I just tell 'em
whatever number,

08:00.259 --> 08:02.721
And then I disappear
into the produce mist.

08:04.477 --> 08:06.020
Peter? Peter?

08:06.105 --> 08:10.946
Peter (echoing):
There was never peter,
only loose carrots.

08:13.747 --> 08:16.709
The body was discovered
around 9:00 p.M.

08:16.836 --> 08:19.674
Unfortunately, I couldn't
make it down to the crime scene

08:19.760 --> 08:21.220
Because there were no ramps.

08:21.305 --> 08:22.680
Okay, I'm gonna write:

08:22.766 --> 08:24.644
"tonight,
all the streets in this town

08:24.729 --> 08:26.147
Were a dead end."

08:26.233 --> 08:27.691
I never saw the body.

08:27.735 --> 08:29.822
It was cold,
so they sent me on a coffee run.

08:29.949 --> 08:31.992
My lap can
accommodate two trays,

08:32.121 --> 08:33.579
And I can't feel the spills.

08:33.707 --> 08:36.670
"she was found in a creek,
her bosoms frozen solid."

08:36.755 --> 08:40.386
She was a heavyset 60-something
in welder's coveralls.

08:40.472 --> 08:42.891
"no one from beverly hills
had ever been strangled

08:42.978 --> 08:44.813
By their own cheerleader skirt
before."

08:44.940 --> 08:46.232
(gasps)

08:46.402 --> 08:49.239
Wow, I can't believe I'm seeing
how the sausage is made.

08:49.324 --> 08:52.746
Hey, so when you open a book
and you see "random house,"

08:52.832 --> 08:54.877
Is that something
we come up with?

08:54.920 --> 08:57.632
Uh, no, that's-that's
the publisher's name.

08:57.759 --> 08:59.846
I see.
Just drinking it all in.

08:59.931 --> 09:01.975
And what about the list of
cities you see under that name?

09:02.060 --> 09:05.441
Because I was thinking we should
put new york, paris, kokomo.

09:05.526 --> 09:07.863
Those are just the cities
where the publisher has offices.

09:07.948 --> 09:09.742
And kokomo isn't
a real city, joe.

09:09.870 --> 09:11.747
Try telling the beach boys that.

09:11.832 --> 09:14.252
I don't know what our title
should be yet, but beneath it,

09:14.338 --> 09:17.217
It should say: "soon to be
a major motion picture."

09:17.345 --> 09:19.513
I always buy the book
when I see that.

09:19.599 --> 09:21.017
Why don't we just focus
on the writing?

09:21.144 --> 09:22.479
Oh, hey, you ever see books

09:22.564 --> 09:24.483
Where the edges
of the pages are gold?

09:24.652 --> 09:27.030
-Yeah?
-So cool.

09:32.335 --> 09:33.753
What is going on in here?

09:33.838 --> 09:35.800
Who put price tags
on all the cans?

09:35.885 --> 09:38.137
And why is everything
labeled 69 cents?

09:38.265 --> 09:41.478
<i> Peter (muffled):
 Griffin family grocery is
 currently under renovation.</i>

09:41.648 --> 09:43.525
<i> Please excuse our dust.</i>

09:43.610 --> 09:45.237
Peter? Where are you?

09:45.322 --> 09:47.575
<i> Staring at butts
 from behind a one-way mirror.</i>

09:47.661 --> 09:49.454
And why'd you
rearrange everything?

09:49.581 --> 09:51.083
I just want to find my vitamins.

09:51.210 --> 09:53.714
<i> Cupboard four.
 No, that's cupboard seven.</i>

09:53.799 --> 09:55.426
<i> No, wrong way.</i>

09:55.511 --> 09:57.681
I'm not...
Is it warmer or colder?

09:57.766 --> 09:59.810
<i> Cupboard four.
 Cupboard four.</i>

10:00.731 --> 10:02.274
(alarm blaring)

10:02.401 --> 10:04.696
Ma'am, don't worry,
this happens all the time.

10:04.865 --> 10:06.491
I'm sure you have your receipt.

10:06.577 --> 10:08.287
What? No,
I don't have a receipt.

10:08.372 --> 10:10.751
Okay, then, we're just gonna
go to the office,

10:10.919 --> 10:14.008
Call your parents,
and send you on your way.

10:15.555 --> 10:17.682
-Daddy, I just...
-There are gonna be
some changes around here.

10:17.769 --> 10:19.645
First off, no more lipstick.

10:19.731 --> 10:22.485
That's how
all this trouble started.

10:26.829 --> 10:27.914
Okay,
so we just need the ending.

10:27.999 --> 10:29.124
Who was the murderer?

10:29.210 --> 10:31.922
Oh, I have no idea.
It's a cold case.

10:32.008 --> 10:34.469
That's what makes 'em cold--
no one knows how to solve 'em.

10:34.555 --> 10:35.722
Well, how do we finish our novel

10:35.808 --> 10:38.186
If we don't know what happened
in real life?

10:38.271 --> 10:39.689
-Ghost cop.
-No.

10:39.775 --> 10:40.817
Do you know what this means?

10:40.944 --> 10:42.821
We're gonna put on
our sherlock holmes hats

10:42.990 --> 10:44.992
And solve the murder ourselves?

10:45.078 --> 10:47.456
Deerstalker hats, joe.
But yes.

10:47.542 --> 10:50.170
Stupid nonwriter!

10:53.012 --> 10:54.922
Okay, brian, now,
when you're visiting

10:54.975 --> 10:56.476
The family of a deceased victim,

10:56.603 --> 10:57.980
You need to hold a hat
over your chest.

10:58.065 --> 10:59.357
It shows you care.

10:59.484 --> 11:01.529
All I have is this crown
from our burger king lunch.

11:01.656 --> 11:02.948
Hat's a hat.

11:04.245 --> 11:07.040
How can I help you,
officer and your highness?

11:07.201 --> 11:10.883
Hi, yes. We're here with many
questions about your daughter.

11:10.968 --> 11:12.678
You know, the dead one?
You-you remember her?

11:12.763 --> 11:14.390
We'd love any details.

11:14.476 --> 11:16.520
Is this some sort of sick joke?

11:16.606 --> 11:17.856
I assure you it's not, ma'am.

11:17.941 --> 11:19.693
We're writing
a future hit novel

11:19.778 --> 11:20.863
Based on your daughter's murder.

11:20.990 --> 11:22.282
We just need to know who did it.

11:22.327 --> 11:24.997
And, between us, it'd be great
if one of you did.

11:25.082 --> 11:26.751
What is this?
What do you want?

11:26.836 --> 11:28.630
Did you know
jonbenét ramsey's dad

11:28.715 --> 11:31.260
Dated natalee holloway's mom?

11:31.346 --> 11:32.847
What does that have to do
with our case?

11:32.933 --> 11:34.768
Well, nothing,
it's just kind of weird, right?

11:34.853 --> 11:37.816
Do you happen to have
any grainy video footage

11:37.902 --> 11:40.907
Of her singing an emotional song
at a talent show?

11:40.992 --> 11:42.409
Maybe green day's
"time of your life"?

11:42.538 --> 11:45.416
That would really bust
this project wide open for us.

11:45.585 --> 11:47.547
You're both unwell.

11:49.009 --> 11:50.386
Well, that was a bust.

11:50.513 --> 11:53.100
Sorry, I've been holding this in
since burger king.

11:53.185 --> 11:55.063
Oh, seriously? You're just
gonna leave that there?

11:55.190 --> 11:57.860
These people have suffered
a terrible loss.

11:57.988 --> 12:00.116
At least cover it with leaves
or something.

12:00.285 --> 12:01.618
Ugh, fine.

12:05.296 --> 12:06.964
Joe, look.
I found something.

12:07.926 --> 12:10.346
-It's a key to a storage unit.
-How do you know that?

12:10.432 --> 12:12.893
Yeah, me and bonnie have been
doing a fun role-play thing

12:13.021 --> 12:14.939
Where she dresses up
like a sexy maid

12:15.025 --> 12:18.155
And then locks me in a storage
unit while guys come over.

12:18.240 --> 12:20.117
-Oh.
-Yeah, it's pretty kinky.

12:20.245 --> 12:23.207
I, uh, I play the role of
a sexy armoire,

12:23.293 --> 12:24.794
Waiting in another room.

12:24.880 --> 12:27.675
Sounds like she just wants you
out of the house for a while.

12:27.762 --> 12:30.097
Nah. No.

12:35.110 --> 12:37.155
It's okay, lois.
It's a big store.

12:37.282 --> 12:38.867
You may not even run into peter.

12:38.994 --> 12:41.915
Good morning.
How much are the mussels?

12:42.001 --> 12:44.170
$34 a month
at bally's total fitness.

12:44.255 --> 12:45.632
-(bell chimes)
-peter?

12:45.759 --> 12:47.302
Why are you
behind the fish counter?

12:47.346 --> 12:50.476
I got a promotion,
emphasis on the "otion."

12:50.603 --> 12:51.895
-(bell chimes)
-fine.

12:51.980 --> 12:53.607
What do you got that's fresh?

12:53.734 --> 12:55.152
Well, I got
a teenage son at home.

12:55.196 --> 12:57.073
-What a mouth on that kid.
-(bell chimes)

12:57.159 --> 12:59.913
That's it! You have
ruined groceries for me!

13:00.040 --> 13:02.377
Get the hell out of my store,
you imbecile!

13:02.462 --> 13:05.383
Um, excuse me, miss, did you
just yell at this employee?

13:05.511 --> 13:06.886
You're damn right I did.

13:06.972 --> 13:09.016
He has no business being here.

13:09.102 --> 13:11.647
This man is a member
of the stop 'n shop family.

13:11.774 --> 13:13.860
He has every business
being here.

13:13.946 --> 13:16.031
You, on the other hand,
will have to go.

13:16.159 --> 13:17.326
You're banned from the store.

13:17.412 --> 13:19.038
(chuckles nervously):
What? No.

13:19.166 --> 13:20.332
Y-you can't do this.

13:20.418 --> 13:22.211
I have shopped here
my whole life.

13:22.339 --> 13:24.300
Yes, we know.
If it's any consolation,

13:24.385 --> 13:26.095
You'll be in
the "in memoriam" section

13:26.222 --> 13:28.016
Of the grocery store oscars.

13:28.101 --> 13:29.896
("I will remember you"
by sarah mclachlan playing)

13:30.023 --> 13:35.867
<i>♪ I will remember you ♪</i>

13:37.038 --> 13:42.088
<i>-♪ will you remember me? ♪
-(cheering)</i>

13:43.344 --> 13:46.556
<i>-♪ don't let your life... ♪
-(man coughs)</i>

13:46.684 --> 13:49.522
<i>Lois: No! No, no, no. You can't
 put me after betty white.</i>

13:49.607 --> 13:51.902
Didn't brenda vaccaro die
or something?

13:51.987 --> 13:53.489
(gasps) no.

13:53.574 --> 13:56.830
I live here in aisle four
with the kotex tampons.

13:56.915 --> 13:58.959
(wheezing)

13:59.086 --> 14:00.838
Still more absorbent
than the leading brand.

14:00.966 --> 14:02.424
(wheezing)

14:08.314 --> 14:10.150
The worst part is,
I can't even go back

14:10.278 --> 14:12.029
To my favorite grocery store.

14:12.156 --> 14:14.618
I personally think
you should give peter a taste

14:14.787 --> 14:18.167
Of his own medicine and
get a job at his special place.

14:18.253 --> 14:20.172
The men's room at logan airport?

14:20.216 --> 14:21.968
No, the drunken clam.

14:22.053 --> 14:24.264
Oh, okay, 'cause he had
this one experience there

14:24.392 --> 14:26.018
That he still talks about
to this day,

14:26.104 --> 14:28.816
But that is an intriguing idea,
bonnie.

14:28.943 --> 14:30.278
I'm glad you think so.

14:30.363 --> 14:32.950
Well, as white women
in conversation,

14:33.036 --> 14:34.954
We're now obligated
to spend five minutes

14:35.040 --> 14:36.875
Talking about sedona, arizona.

14:37.003 --> 14:38.671
-Oh, I'd love to go.
-I know.

14:38.757 --> 14:42.095
My friend linda got a massage
there after her divorce.

14:42.222 --> 14:44.183
And my friend trish
bought a painting there.

14:44.268 --> 14:46.647
-Oh, we got to go.
-We got to go.

14:50.449 --> 14:53.370
Hey, you two haven't
seen peter, have you?

14:53.413 --> 14:55.416
Asking as a waitress
trying to teach him a lesson

14:55.502 --> 14:58.214
By working at his favorite
place, not as his wife.

14:58.299 --> 15:01.053
Whoa, check out the turd-cutter
on the new chick.

15:01.138 --> 15:03.058
That's right.
I work here now.

15:03.185 --> 15:05.187
I'm gonna be here all the time.

15:05.272 --> 15:07.150
Oh, how does it feel
to have someone invade

15:07.277 --> 15:08.904
Your special space?

15:08.990 --> 15:10.198
It feels great!

15:10.325 --> 15:11.910
Speaking of
invading special places,

15:11.996 --> 15:13.038
How about this?

15:13.165 --> 15:15.084
Hey, sweetie,
when do you get off work?

15:15.211 --> 15:17.464
Me and my wife are more friends
at this point than anything.

15:17.550 --> 15:19.010
Don't get me wrong,
she's a great gal,

15:19.095 --> 15:20.930
Raised my children,
but time takes its toll,

15:21.057 --> 15:22.099
You know what I mean?

15:22.226 --> 15:23.728
What? My wife and I have
an arrangement,

15:23.855 --> 15:26.443
So I'm not doing anything
wrong here, technically.

15:26.528 --> 15:28.488
Ah, well, this isn't working.

15:28.532 --> 15:30.827
If you want to meet me
in my car later,

15:30.912 --> 15:33.291
It's the one with
the "blue lives matter" sticker.

15:33.376 --> 15:36.506
But, like, not for cops,
it's for, it's for grover.

15:40.768 --> 15:42.268
Who's going in first?

15:42.353 --> 15:44.607
Kind of feels like you should
since you're a dog.

15:44.692 --> 15:45.860
Are you scared, joe?

15:45.987 --> 15:47.906
Would a scared person do this?

15:47.991 --> 15:50.871
-(screams)
-not so fast.

15:50.956 --> 15:53.042
<i> (serial theme playing)</i>

15:53.127 --> 15:54.545
Who is that?

15:54.631 --> 15:56.634
<i>I'm guessing
it's the lady from serial.</i>

15:56.719 --> 16:00.266
Oh, I certainly wouldn't
recognize a podcaster visually.

16:00.435 --> 16:02.939
-I'm sarah koenig.
-Big fan of your work.

16:03.024 --> 16:05.653
No one turns another person's
suffering into profit better.

16:05.780 --> 16:08.952
Listen up, I want this case
for my podcast,

16:09.037 --> 16:10.288
So you need to drop it.

16:10.374 --> 16:12.961
And if you don't,
I could make you disappear.

16:13.046 --> 16:15.291
We're sponsored
by casper mattresses.

16:15.343 --> 16:17.721
That wasn't a threat.
I have a code if you want it.

16:17.807 --> 16:19.976
Man:
Stand down, sarah.

16:20.061 --> 16:21.856
I'm keith morrison,

16:21.983 --> 16:24.611
<i>And I want this case
for dateline.</i>

16:24.738 --> 16:28.035
There are only a few hundred
unsolved murders left,

16:28.121 --> 16:31.835
And there's a million
true crime content creators.

16:31.963 --> 16:34.383
My grandson taught me that term.

16:34.510 --> 16:37.472
Who's "okay, boomer" now?

16:38.560 --> 16:41.440
We're npr's team
of women with lisps

16:41.525 --> 16:43.569
And names nobody's ever had,

16:43.655 --> 16:47.453
Like sylvia delgado-smith,
and audie takahashi o'shea.

16:47.580 --> 16:49.541
<i>I'm chris hansen
from to catch a predator,</i>

16:49.668 --> 16:51.712
And I'm just here
in case any of you

16:51.797 --> 16:53.049
Turn out to be pedophiles.

16:53.134 --> 16:55.345
Warm chocolate chip cookie,
anyone?

16:55.473 --> 16:58.060
<i>No! I claimed this cold case
for serial.</i>

16:58.145 --> 17:01.609
<i>Not if I record a dateline
first.</i>

17:02.112 --> 17:04.616
(all grunting)

17:10.756 --> 17:12.508
(choking)

17:12.593 --> 17:14.553
♪ ♪

17:17.061 --> 17:18.437
(screaming)

17:18.564 --> 17:20.483
(grunting)

17:28.211 --> 17:31.508
Please...
Rate and review my life.

17:31.593 --> 17:33.846
And someone take care of my dog

17:33.931 --> 17:36.894
You could usually hear
in the background of my podcast.

17:36.980 --> 17:38.940
(gasping)

17:39.110 --> 17:40.277
(grunting)

17:41.281 --> 17:44.328
A foggy night
at a storage unit in quahog.

17:44.371 --> 17:47.250
The sleepy little town of quahog

17:47.336 --> 17:51.051
Is usually all tucked in
by 10:00 p.M.

17:51.136 --> 17:53.180
(clamoring)

17:53.266 --> 17:55.143
You know what?
We're no better than them.

17:55.270 --> 17:57.022
We've been exploiting
the victim's life

17:57.107 --> 17:58.734
For our own personal gain.

17:58.819 --> 18:01.031
I-I think it's time for us
to abandon writing this book.

18:01.116 --> 18:05.248
Or... Maybe we set it to rap
lyrics and take it to broadway?

18:05.417 --> 18:07.252
I think we're done here.

18:08.424 --> 18:10.259
You know, joe,
even though it didn't work out,

18:10.387 --> 18:12.013
It was nice to spend
some time with someone

18:12.140 --> 18:13.642
Who actually believed
in my writing.

18:13.727 --> 18:17.525
Well, as someone who's never
read a book, I absolutely do.

18:21.160 --> 18:24.290
The waitress from the clam!
Holy crap, has lois seen you?!

18:24.376 --> 18:25.418
We really don't have
an arrangement.

18:25.545 --> 18:26.420
You got to get out of here!

18:26.547 --> 18:27.965
Oh, peter, enough.

18:28.050 --> 18:30.262
-What's the matter?
-You wouldn't understand.

18:30.305 --> 18:32.599
Okay.

18:33.980 --> 18:36.024
I'd get back in there, chief.

18:37.195 --> 18:39.740
(sighs) chris made me come back.

18:39.826 --> 18:41.996
Oh, honey,
the grocery store isn't just

18:42.081 --> 18:44.125
Where I buy food for the family.

18:44.210 --> 18:45.462
It's my escape.

18:45.547 --> 18:47.716
My refuge
from being pestered

18:47.802 --> 18:49.219
With dumb questions
from the kids,

18:49.305 --> 18:50.973
Or having to clean up
your messes.

18:51.100 --> 18:54.314
Sometimes, just a stroll
down the ethnic food aisle

18:54.399 --> 18:56.861
Makes me feel like
I'm in a north african bazaar.

18:56.989 --> 18:58.866
Yeah, I don't like the smells
on that aisle.

18:59.035 --> 19:02.207
-And I don't know,
it's hard to explain, but...
-There's more?!

19:02.292 --> 19:04.879
It's not just
a grocery store to me.

19:04.964 --> 19:07.050
There's a whole
community of people there

19:07.136 --> 19:08.553
Who feel like family.

19:08.639 --> 19:11.017
And now,
now I have nothing.

19:11.102 --> 19:15.235
Aw, lois, I'm so sorry
for ruining your happy place.

19:15.320 --> 19:17.072
And I'm gonna take care of it.

19:17.158 --> 19:19.494
Just like I've been taking care
of that egg since high school.

19:19.664 --> 19:22.459
Oh, my god, I forgot to pick
him up from soccer practice!

19:23.380 --> 19:26.426
Hey, do you need me
to call your yolks?

19:29.226 --> 19:30.811
Look, you got to let lois
come back.

19:30.896 --> 19:33.233
Please remove the ban.
She loves this place.

19:33.318 --> 19:34.485
I'm sorry, but I can't do that.

19:34.571 --> 19:36.949
She yelled at
a mentally-challenged person,

19:37.034 --> 19:38.076
And that's unforgivable.

19:38.246 --> 19:39.621
What?
I'm not mentally challenged.

19:39.707 --> 19:41.543
You're not?
But that's literally

19:41.628 --> 19:43.505
The only reason we hired you.

19:43.549 --> 19:47.013
Would a mentally challenged
person be able to do this?

19:51.232 --> 19:53.569
Your name tag says "big petey."

19:53.654 --> 19:55.656
(scoffs) why do you think
we all gather round

19:55.784 --> 19:57.411
And applaud you while you ride

19:57.455 --> 19:59.039
The coin-operated horse
out front?

19:59.125 --> 20:00.375
'cause I'm good at horses?

20:00.461 --> 20:02.797
Wow. (chuckles)
I really thought...

20:02.883 --> 20:05.178
You know, we don't let
all our employees insist

20:05.305 --> 20:08.059
The customers feel their muscles
after bagging their order.

20:08.102 --> 20:09.312
Right?

20:09.439 --> 20:10.481
Okay, fine.

20:10.608 --> 20:12.443
Lois can come back,
but you're fired.

20:12.529 --> 20:14.281
I need you to turn in
your gun and badge.

20:14.450 --> 20:16.870
Well, I guess
my work here is done.

20:16.997 --> 20:18.666
To the mickey-copter!

20:21.340 --> 20:22.465
See, disney?

20:22.550 --> 20:24.637
Nothing here
but respectful synergy.

20:33.826 --> 20:35.911
What happened to
the open floor plan?

20:36.039 --> 20:38.626
Long story. The wework guy
took our entire budget

20:38.753 --> 20:41.005
For the project
as a holiday bonus.

20:41.050 --> 20:43.177
But he has long hair
and speaks confidently

20:43.221 --> 20:44.304
About the internet,

20:44.391 --> 20:46.309
So he will get about
eight more chances.

20:46.395 --> 20:48.982
Ah, yes, the wework guy.

20:49.067 --> 20:53.450
They thought he had created
a $47 billion unicorn.

20:53.535 --> 20:56.832
Turns out it was only
a two-bit donkey.

20:56.960 --> 20:58.920
That's wet paint,
by the way.

20:59.883 --> 21:01.176
Ah, son of a...